{"name":"Scroll of Wisdom","hex":"#f3e5c0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scroll","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A roll of paper or parchment; a writing formed into a roll.","An ornament formed of undulations giving off spirals or sprays, usually suggestive of plant form. Roman architectural ornament is largely of some scroll pattern."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To change one's view of data on a computer's display by moving in gradual increments, typically using an input device or touch screen.","To move in or out of view horizontally or vertically."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scroll"},{"term":"wisdom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An element of personal character that enables one to distinguish the wise from the unwise.","A piece of wise advice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wisdom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scroll","blocks":[{"text":"A scroll, also known as a roll, is a roll of papyrus, parchment, or paper containing writing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Joshua_Roll.jpg/330px-Joshua_Roll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scroll"},{"title":"Wisdom","blocks":[{"text":"Wisdom, also known as sapience, is defined by psychologists as a combination of \"wit and virtue,\" the ability to apply expert tacit and experiential knowledge, balancing intrapersonal, interpersonal and institutional interests, to deal with complex questions of life and attain a common good. Wisdom can be viewed as a stable personality trait, but also as context-bound process, meaning that a person in some contexts behaves wisely, but in other contexts does not. Wisdom can also be viewed as influenced and determined by sociocultural norms and traditions. Wisdom can be viewed solely as wise behaviour, describing actions which lead to \"an altruistic outcome by creatively and successfully solving problems.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Luca_Giordano_-_Dream_of_Solomon_-_WGA09004.jpg/330px-Luca_Giordano_-_Dream_of_Solomon_-_WGA09004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisdom"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Scroll.jpg/330px-Scroll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Scroll.jpg/330px-Scroll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scroll of the Book of Esther, Seville, Spain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScroll.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Scroll_ink_materials.JPG/500px-Scroll_ink_materials.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Scroll_ink_materials.JPG/500px-Scroll_ink_materials.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ingredients used in making ink for Hebrew scrolls today","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScroll_ink_materials.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Volumen_y_Rotulus.jpg/250px-Volumen_y_Rotulus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Volumen_y_Rotulus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Volumen_y_Rotulus.jpg/250px-Volumen_y_Rotulus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Volumen and Rotulus, two types of scrolls","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVolumen_y_Rotulus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t